# Blog Route — AI Agent Reference

Purpose of this doc: give any AI agent full context on the dynamic blog content
system so it can make edits/additions without needing to read every file.
Site: mirelleinspo.com (Next.js App Router).

---

## 1. Route Map

| Route | File | Renders |
|---|---|---|
| `/blog` | `src/app/blog/page.tsx` | Blog listing/homepage (hero, carousels, must-read, latest, pagination) |
| `/blog/[slug]` | `src/app/blog/[...slug]/page.tsx` | Single post (standalone or pillar) OR Topic Hub if slug is a pillar |
| `/blog/[topic]/[slug]` | same catch-all file | Single post nested under a topic |

Single catch-all: `src/app/blog/[...slug]/page.tsx` handles both 1-segment and
2-segment URLs based on `segments.length`.

---

## 2. Data Source

Posts live as `.md` / `.mdx` files in `src/content/blogs/`, either flat or in
topic subfolders (e.g. `src/content/blogs/skin-tone/best-nude-nail-color-for-skin-tone.md`).

- `.md` → compiled to HTML at request time via `marked` (in `blog.ts`)
- `.mdx` → raw source passed to `<MDXRemote>` (rendered via `MDXContent.tsx`)

Frontmatter fields (used across the system): `title, excerpt, date, author,
category, image, imageAlt, imageWidth, imageHeight, readTime, topic, canonical,
template, topicalMap, navigationContext, carouselImages, products, tldr,
faqItems, dateModified, wordCount, tags`.

`template` value picks the render template: `center | split-left | split-right | grid`.

### topicalMap (pillar/cluster system)
```
topicalMap: {
  position: 'pillar' | 'cluster' | 'standalone',
  parentPillar: string | null   // pillar's slug, for cluster posts
}
```
- A **pillar** post + its **cluster** posts form a "topic family."
- Visiting `/blog/[pillarSlug]` (1 segment, no matching post slug conflict)
  renders the **Topic Hub** (`PillarHub` component) instead of a post — a
  listing of the pillar + all its clusters.
- Visiting `/blog/[topic]/[slug]` always renders the actual post.

