## 5. Page: `src/app/blog/[...slug]/page.tsx` (post / hub page)

### `generateStaticParams`
Builds static paths for every post: `[topic, slug]` if post has a topic, plus
`[topic]` alone for pillar posts (registers the hub route). Falls back to
just `[slug]` if no topic.

### `generateMetadata`
- 1 segment + matches a pillar → hub metadata (`robots: {index:false, follow:true}` — hub is nav-only, not indexed)
- 1 segment + matches a post → `buildPostMetadata()`
- 2 segments → looks up post by `postSlug` (ignores topic in URL for lookup, but 404s later if topic doesn't match), → `buildPostMetadata()`

`buildPostMetadata(post, canonicalUrl, imageUrl, imageAltText)` — builds the
full Next.js `Metadata` object: OG tags, Twitter card, `article:*` meta,
resolves author via `resolveAuthor()` from `src/data/authors.ts`.

### Default export `BlogCatchAllPage`
Routes to `PillarHub` (if segment matches a pillar slug) or `PostPage`
(otherwise), with 404 via `notFound()` for unmatched/mismatched cases.

### `PostPage({ post, slug })`
1. Calls `generateSchemas({ post, slug })` from `src/lib/generateSchemas.ts`
2. Injects JSON-LD `<script>` tags: article, breadcrumb, + conditional faq/howTo/video/imageGallery schemas
3. Picks template component from map: `{ center, 'split-left', 'split-right', grid }` (default `center`)
4. Renders `<Template post={postWithCoverImage} />`

### `PillarHub({ topic })`
Renders topic hub: pillar title/excerpt + grid of `Link` cards (pillar card
first, then all cluster posts), linking to `/blog/${topic}/${slug}`.

